course: dictionary
lesson: 13722
title: Insufficiency: not having enough
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Insufficiency is a noun. It means not having enough of something. You can also say an insufficiency of something, which is a more formal way of saying there is a shortage.
explain: «The cake failed because there was an insufficiency of sugar.» The cake did not work because there was not enough sugar. Look at the words around insufficiency to check: failed and sugar show that something was missing.
explain: In maths, an insufficiency of information means you cannot find the answer, because some facts are missing. In medicine, doctors use the word for a body part that does not work well enough, such as «kidney insufficiency».
fact: Insufficiency means not having enough of something.
fact: «An insufficiency of information» means there are not enough facts to solve a problem.
fact: In medicine, insufficiency is when a body part does not work well enough, like «heart insufficiency».
fact: Insufficiency is a formal word, so you will often see it in writing rather than in chatty talk.
fact: A simple swap helps: if you can put «not enough» into the sentence and it still makes sense, insufficiency is the right meaning.
exercise: «The cake failed because there was an insufficiency of sugar.» What does insufficiency mean here? | *Not enough sugar | Sugar in a box | A very sweet taste | Too much sugar
exercise: «The maths problem gave an insufficiency of information, so Sam could not find the answer.» Why could Sam not find the answer? | *There was not enough information | He forgot his pencil | The answer was too big | Sam could not add up
exercise: Doctors say «kidney insufficiency» when a body part does what? | *Does not work well enough | Glows in the dark | Grows too fast | Changes colour
test: Which phrase means there is not enough money? | *An insufficiency of money | A great deal of money | A surplus of money | Plenty of money
test: In which sentence is insufficiency used correctly? | The river had an insufficiency of water, so it was full | *The team had an insufficiency of players, so the match could not start | The cake had an insufficiency of colour, so it was bright | The sky had an insufficiency of clouds, so it rained
exam: Which sentence uses insufficiency correctly? | *The class had an insufficiency of books, so pupils shared | The book had an insufficiency of pages, so it was very thick | The insufficiency of the sun made the room bright | The insufficiency of the bus was on time
